  "answer": "Your Strength note now has an app on its App side, and the check found no problems. It opens on the first day with sets still to do. You can step through the days with the arrows or jump to any day from the program list. Each set is a button you tap to tick or untick, and each day shows how many sets are done.\n\nThe whole program is in the app's data, not the note text, and your ticks are saved there too. The block starts on 12 October and the days are dated from that.\n\nI read your program like this:\n- **Week 2:** every lift is 2.5 kg heavier than week 1.\n- **Week 3:** every lift is 5 kg heavier than week 1.\n- **Week 4:** every lift is 2×5 at week 1 weights. That includes deadlift, which becomes 2×5 instead of 1×5, and row, which becomes 2×5 instead of 3×8. Say if you'd rather keep those two as they were.\n\nI named the lifts \"Barbell row\" and \"Overhead press\", since you wrote \"row\" and \"press\".",
